cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal artifact, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Designability of RNA Targets with Up to Two Length-2 Helices"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jogalekar
    given-names: Ashutosh S.
    affiliation: "Szilard Scientific, LLC"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formal artifact and manuscript for a theorem in the pseudoknot-free
  four-letter Watson-Crick maximum-base-pair model with zero minimum base-pair
  span: every target with no maximal helix of length 1, at most two maximal
  helices of length 2, all other maximal helices of length at least 3, and no
  m5 or m3-dot obstruction motif is uniquely designable.
version: "1.0.3"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22101755"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ajogalekar/rna-at-most-two-short-helices"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22101755"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - RNA inverse folding
  - RNA design
  - secondary structure
  - Watson-Crick model
  - isolated stack
  - separated coloring
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4 theorem proving
